; Exercise 3: V0 := V1 times V2 by adding V1 to V0, V2 times. The loop is
; four instructions, with its test at the bottom; a test before it sends
; V2 = 0 straight to the end. For 6 times 7 the loop runs 7 times, the
; last time without its jump back: 4 * 6 + 3 = 27 instructions, and 4
; before them. The product is drawn in decimal, as samples/answer.hex does.

6106    ; 200  V1 := 6
6207    ; 202  V2 := 7
6000    ; 204  V0 := 0
4200    ; 206  skip if V2 is not 0
1214    ; 208  V2 is 0: to the end
8014    ; 20A  V0 += V1             loop:
72FF    ; 20C  V2 -= 1
3200    ; 20E  skip if V2 = 0
120A    ; 210  back to the loop
A300    ; 212  I := 300
F033    ; 214  the digits of V0 at 300, 301, 302
F265    ; 216  V0, V1, V2 := the three digits
6314    ; 218  V3 := 20             x
640C    ; 21A  V4 := 12             y
F029    ; 21C  digit V0
D345    ; 21E
7305    ; 220
F129    ; 222  digit V1
D345    ; 224
7305    ; 226
F229    ; 228  digit V2
D345    ; 22A
122C    ; 22C  the end
